    {
     "tipo": "dialogo",
     "titulo": "Dialogue: evaluating arguments",
     "frases": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "关于「条件与假设」，你觉得哪种证据最有说服力？",
       "alumno": "About «conditions and assumptions», what kind of evidence do you find most convincing?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "我查了几份材料，发现不同来源的说法并不完全一样。",
       "alumno": "I have looked at several materials and found that the sources don't entirely agree.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "你打算怎样核实？",
       "alumno": "How do you plan to check it?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "我会先比较出处，再看论据是否一致。",
       "alumno": "I'll first compare the sources, and then see whether the arguments match.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "林娜",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "如果核实后仍有差异呢？",
       "alumno": "What if the differences remain after checking?",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "王明",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       "estudio": "那就说明不同观点，并把证据的局限写清楚。",
       "alumno": "Then I will set out the different views and make clear the limits of the evidence.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "tipo": "texto",
     "titulo": "Reading: evaluating arguments",
     "frases": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "讨论「条件与假设」时，要区分事实、推论和个人立场。",
       "alumno": "When discussing «conditions and assumptions», you must distinguish facts, inferences and personal positions.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "说明证据的来源并回应反例，结论才更有说服力。",
       "alumno": "Explaining where the evidence comes from and responding to counterexamples strengthens the conclusion.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "如果只凭个人印象，容易忽略其他情况；因此要核对材料，并说明判断依据。",
       "alumno": "If you rely only on personal impressions, you may overlook other cases; that's why you should check the materials and explain the basis for your judgement.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      },
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "组织短文时，可以先提出观点，再用事实或例子支持它。",
       "alumno": "When organising a short text, you can first put forward a view and then support it with facts or examples.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [],
       "parrafo": 0
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
